# Chroma library, modern Earth: bold ways, batch 8 (stage A, 2026-10-18). Each life event below gets a first bold way,
# sometimes a second in another colour, and two links (well and badly) one to three years on, each with its own bold way.
# Played only in played lives (BOLD and LINKS in earth_play.py). Syntax: header of build.py; brief: bold/BRIEF.md.

# ================================================================ living with a chronic illness

== bold: living with a chronic illness / B
base: fit it into your days on your own terms, and ask nobody for favours
likelier_if: years [keeping fit] 3 +10; mark 'learned a skill' +5
- B | enter the town's long race, and finish it to show the illness its place | v: achievement, self-direction | act: enter the town's long race and finish it, to show the illness its place | chance: 35 | grants: trophies won | takes_if_fails: car
works: {N} crosses the line in a good time, and the finisher's medal goes on the shelf beside the pills.
works: The doctor shakes {Ns} hand at the next check-up, and the medal from the race is the first of several.
fails: Halfway round a bad spell puts {N} down on the kerb, the doctor forbids driving after the scare, and the car is sold by the spring.
fails: {N} has to stop a mile from the finish, the illness flares, and with the doctor forbidding driving for a long while the car has to go.

== bold: living with a chronic illness / G
base: accept it as your lot, and make room for it without a fuss
likelier_if: has [old family name] +10; mark 'came home' +5
- G | sell the house in town, and move to a cottage at the edge of the woods | v: tradition, universalism | act: sell the house in town and move to a cottage at the edge of the woods | chance: 40 | grants: knowing the woods | takes_if_fails: homeowner
works: {N} settles in the cottage by the trees, walks the paths every morning, and learns which ones the body can manage on a bad day.
works: The woods become {Ns} doctor's second opinion: {N} knows every path, every spring and every bench, and the illness settles.
fails: The town house sells, but the cottage falls through at the last moment, and {N} ends up renting a flat on the ring road.
fails: The move goes wrong after the sale, prices by the woods have climbed out of reach, and {N} is a tenant from then on.

== the Sunday runners
tier: link
of_bold: living with a chronic illness / B
side: well
delay: 1-2
holds: trophies won
stages: juvenile+
age: 13-100
stakes: .6
tone: joy
life: body, health, friends
horizon: months
roles: friend
earth: since your race, others with the same illness want you to lead them on Sunday runs
scene: Since the race, people with the same illness have started writing to {N}. {friend}, newly diagnosed, asks if {N} would lead a few of them round the park on Sunday mornings.
scene gone: {friend}, who first asked, has moved away. The letters keep coming, though, and the clinic asks {N} to take the Sunday runners on.
- W | agree a plan with the clinic, and have every runner checked by a doctor first | v: security, conformity | chance: 75
- U | work out a training plan that suits the illness, and share it with them all | v: self-direction, benevolence | chance: 78
- B | find a sponsor for the group, with your name on the shirts | v: achievement, power | act: find a sponsor for the group, with their own name on the shirts | chance: 70
- R | just turn up on Sunday and run with whoever comes | v: stimulation, hedonism | chance: 85
- G | take them along the old river path you have run since you were young | v: tradition, benevolence | act: take them along the old river path they have run since they were young | chance: 80
works: By the summer a small crowd meets at the park gate every Sunday, and {N} knows them all by name.
works: {friend} runs a whole lap without stopping, and the group keeps going.
fails: The group shrinks to two after a wet month, and {N} runs alone again.
fails: The runs turn into a chore, and {N} starts to dread Sundays.
works gone: By the summer a small crowd meets at the park gate every Sunday, and {N} knows them all by name.
works gone: The newest runner manages a whole lap without stopping, and the group keeps going.
fails gone: The group shrinks to two after a wet month, and {N} runs alone again.
fails gone: The runs turn into a chore, and {N} starts to dread Sundays.

== bold: the Sunday runners / W
base: agree a plan with the clinic, and have every runner checked by a doctor first
likelier_if: has [organising people] +10; years [keeping fit] 5 +5
- W | take the group on as its organiser, and be there every Sunday, rain or shine | v: conformity, benevolence | act: take the group on as its organiser and be there every Sunday, rain or shine | chance: 40 | requires: keeping fit | title: neighbourhood volunteer | takes_if_fails: keeping fit
works: {N} becomes the group's organiser, with the list of names, the key to the clinic's back room and a place on the town's volunteer rota.
works: The Sunday runners become a fixture, and the town counts {N} among its volunteers.
fails: Too many cold Sundays in a row wear {N} down, the illness flares, and {Ns} own running ends.
fails: {N} pushes on through a bad patch to keep the group going, and the doctor rules out hard running for good.

